          "archive": "agent-fixtures/packaging-prerelease-bounds/source.tar.gz",
          "archive_sha256": "b31d789d50ff7910665e919cf1780dac0a77131d9d0dd9651ecb2bc6281671bd",
          "candidate_root": "src/packaging",
          "id": "packaging-prerelease-bounds",
          "oracle_root": "private/task2/evaluator",
          "prompt": "Fix implicit prerelease admission for strict version bounds in Packaging.\n\nWhen the bound itself is a prerelease or development release, strict greater-than and less-than specifiers must participate in prerelease detection and filtering consistently with the public API contract. Examples:\n\n- Specifier(\">1.0.dev1\").prereleases and Specifier(\"<1.0.dev1\").prereleases must be True.\n- Specifier(\">3.0.0a7\").contains(\"3.0.0a8\") and Specifier(\"<3.0.0a8\").contains(\"3.0.0a7\") must be True.\n- list(Specifier(\">2.0a1\").filter([\"2.0a1\", \"3.0a2\", \"3.0\"])) must equal [\"3.0a2\", \"3.0\"].\n\nExcluding a prerelease with != must not implicitly enable prereleases. Preserve explicit prerelease overrides and ordinary non-prerelease comparisons. Make the production fix and add suitable regression coverage. Work only in this checkout; do not retrieve upstream patches or history. Report the changes and tests you ran. The external evaluator restores its frozen upstream test suite, so weakening checkout tests cannot satisfy evaluation.\n",
          "pytest_selection": null,
          "regression": "tests",
          "replace_regression_tests": "private/task2/evaluator/tests"
        }
